{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/449496-rites-and-you-or-you-and-your-rites","id":449496,"title":"Rites and You, or You and Your Rites","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-19T11:36:37-07:00","id":449496,"title":"Rites and You, or You and Your Rites","content":"Many of us have had access to the book for a while, some are probably playing. So I wanted to ask what you've done or seen done with personalized rites. Have you stuck to the sample rites, or has your character developed something more fitting for themselves?<br /> <br /> If you don't have the book, it was discussed during one of <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/ritualistic/\" target=\"_blank\">Stew Wilson's blogs during development</a>. Essentially, rites are personalized for the character or pack, so while some might perform a very 'tribal' ceremony to start the Sacred Hunt rite, others might get together, get drunk and throw darts at a picture or drawing of their target, so that your pack doesn't have to break from their lifestyle and pretend to be shamans if they're technophiles or have any other predilections.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T12:49:16-07:00","id":449593,"title":"","content":"I haven't started playing yet, but I gave some thought to the Bottle Spirit rite that I'm planning for my character to have.<br /> The elements involved are bottles, stasis, air, and death.<br /> The rite would involve two main steps. First, I would scratch or draw or otherwise inscribe upon the bottle to be used a number of arcane runes for binding and holding. With that done, I would set it down a few feet away from a fire. I would then hold up a set of wind chimes made of bones that have matching runes inscribed upon them. The chimes, however, have been weighted so that they don't sway with the wind and don't chime.<br /> As the bones cast their shadow on the bottle that will hold the spirit, I'll hold the chimes as still as possible as the wind, my pack mates, and I all attempt to blow them. The stillness of the bones instills the bottle with enough essence of stasis to hold a spirit captive for a day. (Composure + Occult for the stillness and the runes)<br /> <br /> I saw a really good example somewhere where someone was going to call the sacred hunt with Composure + Brawl by having the rite master calmly and stoically pummel an effigy representing the prey into nothingness. It had more deatil than that which I don't remember, but I remember it was impressive and creative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T17:27:27-07:00","id":451099,"title":"","content":"I'm excited to write up a version of Hunting Ground that plays on the concept of &quot;good fences make good neighbors&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently playing at Fabula Rasa in the Cold Equations venue; planning an Obrimos for Fallen London.<br /> I can also be found at <a href=\"http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com\" target=\"_blank\">http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2192-heu","name":"Heu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T17:40:57-07:00","id":451107,"title":"","content":"In Southern folk magic, there is something called a bottle tree which pretty much does the same thing the bottle spirit rite does. That might be a good source of inspiration for the rite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T05:16:16-07:00","id":451439,"title":"","content":"I figure a classic Iron Masters version of the Bottle rite would be to inscribed (or paint, for reusability) an Ocarina of Time cartridge with the symbols of stasis, then start a new game, get a bottle and capture a fairy (spirit). Then a fight to the glorious death, letting the fairy out to heal you. All the while, packmates sit as still as possible around the ritemaster.<br /> <br /> Still not sure how to work air into it.<br /> <br /> Resolve + Computers","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5292-flailbot","name":"FlailBot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T06:38:54-07:00","id":451481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FlailBot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/449496-rites-and-you-or-you-and-your-rites?p=451439#post451439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I figure a classic Iron Masters version of the Bottle rite would be to inscribed (or paint, for reusability) an Ocarina of Time cartridge with the symbols of stasis, then start a new game, get a bottle and capture a fairy (spirit). Then a fight to the glorious death, letting the fairy out to heal you. All the while, packmates sit as still as possible around the ritemaster.<br /> <br /> Still not sure how to work air into it.<br /> <br /> Resolve + Computers</div> </div> </div> </div>Have one of your packmates suck on helium and do a Navi impression. Stillness truly comes from trying not to laugh. Composure+Computers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently playing at Fabula Rasa in the Cold Equations venue; planning an Obrimos for Fallen London.<br /> I can also be found at <a href=\"http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com\" target=\"_blank\">http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2192-heu","name":"Heu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T07:04:10-07:00","id":451488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FlailBot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/449496-rites-and-you-or-you-and-your-rites?p=451439#post451439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I figure a classic Iron Masters version of the Bottle rite would be to inscribed (or paint, for reusability) an Ocarina of Time cartridge with the symbols of stasis, then start a new game, get a bottle and capture a fairy (spirit). Then a fight to the glorious death, letting the fairy out to heal you. All the while, packmates sit as still as possible around the ritemaster.<br /> <br /> Still not sure how to work air into it.<br /> <br /> Resolve + Computers</div> </div> </div> </div>A pop-culture-minded Bone Shadow could try such a... creative ritual practice <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Not an Iron Master, though, as the Bone Shadows jealously guard their knowledge of Bottle Spirit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T09:17:31-07:00","id":451603,"title":"","content":"When I read the rites rules, I checked if I could come up with rituals for a quiet, bookish werewolf. And I saw that it was good.<br /> <br /> Chain Rage: Put on some heavy metal music. Sit on a mat patterned as the flag of Japan. (You know... Land of the Rising Sun.) Ritually &quot;chain&quot; yourself with a <a href=\"https://www.google.ca/search?hl=fr&amp;site=imghp&amp;tbm=isch&amp;source=hp&amp;biw=1230&amp;bih=671&amp;q=chain+bracelet&amp;oq=chain+bracelet&amp;gs_l=img.3..0.1069.3909.0.4230.14.8.0.6.6.0.134.773.2j5.7.0.msedr...0...1ac.1.62.img..1.13.782.3RnxC5pM9mo\" target=\"_blank\">fashionable bracelet</a>. Then start reading philosophy texts and self-help anger management books. Intelligence + Academics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T14:15:06-07:00","id":452014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I saw a really good example somewhere where someone was going to call the sacred hunt with Composure + Brawl by having the rite master calmly and stoically pummel an effigy representing the prey into nothingness. It had more deatil than that which I don't remember, but I remember it was impressive and creative.</div> </div> </div> </div>Either that was me, or I accidentally copied it from somewhere else! :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T20:55:52-07:00","id":452264,"title":"","content":"It might have been, Barbrarilen. If so, way to go. I liked that one.<br /> <br /> Off the topic of rites but on the topic of confusion over sources, I've studiously avoided forums up to now due to a deep seated paranoia or having to riffle through mountains of data to find what you need. As such, my due diligence in citing other things on the forum is likely to be lackluster at best. The same is likely to be true for my memory on exactly who said what. Also, I'm liable to ask questions that have already been answered.<br /> <br /> That all said, I successfully used the search funtcion on the errata thead a few times to avoid posting about things already mentioned. It was a big personal victory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}